(a) Generally. The chairman and members of the board of commissioners of the county shall determine the policies of the county and shall have and exercise all of the powers heretofore granted by general or local law as may be indispensable or incidental to their jurisdiction over county matters which are not otherwise vested in the county manager pursuant to subsection (b)(5) of this section. The chairman shall be the chief executive officer of the board of commissioners.
(b) (1) Position created. Pursuant to the authority granted to the board of commissioners of the county in O.C.G.A. § 36-5-22, there is hereby created the position of county manager of McDuffie County. The county manager shall be the chief manager and head of the administrative branch of county government. The county manager shall serve at the pleasure of the board of commissioners. The board of commissioners of the county shall select and appoint a county manager, who shall receive such compensation as may be prescribed by the board of commissioners. The county manager must devote all of such officer's working time and attention to the affairs of the county and shall be responsible to the board of commissioners for the efficient administration of all the affairs of the county over which such officer has jurisdiction.
(2) Qualifications. No person shall be chosen as county manager unless such person shall be of good character and have proven executive ability and experience. The county manager shall be chosen by the board of commissioners solely on the basis of such person's executive and administrative qualifications. No person shall he appointed as county manager unless such person possesses the following minimum qualifications:
a. A bachelor's degree in business administration or public administration and at least four years' experience in public administration; or
b. A master's degree in business administration or public administration and at least two years' experience in public administration; or
c. At least ten years' experience in public administration as a city or county manager or administrator.
No person elected to any county public office shall, subsequent to such election, be eligible for appointment as county manager until two years have elapsed following the expiration of the term of office for which such person was elected.
(3) Term. The county manager shall be appointed for an indefinite term and shall serve at the pleasure of the board of commissioners. Any action of the board in suspending or removing the county manager shall be final.
(4) Absence, disability or suspension; filling vacancy. The board of commissioners may designate a person or persons to perform the functions and duties of the county manager during the absence, disability, or suspension of the county manager. Vacancies in the office of county manager shall be filled by the board of commissioners as early as practicable, and, until such vacancy is filled, the board of commissioners shall have full power to make a temporary appointment or to perform the functions and duties of such office.
(5) Duties, power and authority. The county manager shall have the following duties, power, and authority:
a. To supervise the administration of the affairs of the county and to see that the ordinances, resolutions and regulations of the board of commissioners and the laws of the state are faithfully executed and enforced;
b. To employ and remove all employees of the county under the jurisdiction of the board of commissioners except the county attorney, county auditor, and members of all the boards, commissions, and authorities, who shall be removed by the board of commissioners;
c. To exercise managerial authority and supervision over all departments and personnel under the jurisdiction of the board of commissioners;
d. To require reports for heads of departments and other employees entrusted with administrative duties or exercising discretion. The county manager shall have at all times the authority to examine all books and records of every officer and department of the county under the jurisdiction of the board of commissioners;
e. To attend all meetings of the board of commissioners with a right to take part in the discussions but having no vote;
f. To recommend to the board of commissioners for adoption such measures as the county manager may deem necessary or expedient;
g. To supervise performance of all contracts made by any person, company, or corporation for work done for the board of commissioners;
h. The county manager, or the authorized designee of the county manager, shall be the purchasing agent of materials and supplies for the county under such rules and regulations as may be imposed by the board of commissioners;
i. The county manager shall, no later than the 20th day of the seventh month of each fiscal year, submit to the board of commissioners a budget plan and calendar for developing a proposed operating budget for the ensuing fiscal year; and the county manager shall formulate and submit to the board of commissioners, no later than the 20th day of the tenth month of each fiscal year, a proposed operating budget for the next fiscal year showing budget revenues and expenditures during the preceding fiscal year; appropriations and estimated revenue and recommended expenditures for the next fiscal year; recommended salaries; proposed capital expenditures; recommended tax levy; and such other information and data as may be considered necessary by the board of commissioners;
j. To keep the board of commissioners fully advised at all times as to the financial condition and needs of the county;
k. To make or cause to be made a full written report to the board of commissioners each month showing the operations and expenditures of each department of the county government for the preceding month;
l. To serve as personnel director in the supervision and administration of the county's personnel system for county employees;
m. To delegate purely administrative duties to subordinates in the county government whose work the county manager shall supervise and direct; provided, however, the delegation or assignment of duties to subordinates shall not relieve the county manager from responsibility for administration of county affairs;
n. To serve as clerk of the board of commissioners of the county; and
o. To perform such other duties as may be prescribed by the ordinance or other duties as may from time to time be required by the board of commissioners.
(6) Bond required. The county manager, before entering upon the discharge of the duties of county manager, shall execute a bond with a solvent surety company licensed to do business in McDuffie County, conditioned for the faithful performance of such officer's duties and to secure against corruption, malfeasance, misappropriation, or unlawful expenditure. The premium on such bond shall be paid for by McDuffie County. The county manager may require subordinate employees to likewise give bond in an amount to be determined by the county manager subject to the approval of the board of commissioners, but not less than $100,000.00. The premiums on such bonds shall be paid for by McDuffie County.
(7) Political engagements. The county manager shall not engage in or be concerned with local partisan politics or any local political campaign. The county manager shall not contribute to any local campaign fund or solicit funds for local political purposes for any other person. The county manager shall not be eligible for election as a member of the board of commissioners of the county for a period of two years after termination of service as a county manager.
(Ord. of 7-7-99, §§ 1, 2; Ord. of 12-21-99, §§ 1, 2; Mo. of 1-18-00)

