(a) "Dangerous animal" shall mean any animal which has:
(1) Caused a substantial puncture of a person's skin by teeth without causing serious injury; provided, however, that a nip, scratch, or abrasion shall not be sufficient to classify an animal as dangerous under this subparagraph;
(2) Aggressively attacked in a manner that causes a person to reasonably believe that the animal posed an imminent threat of serious injury to such person or another person although no such injury occurs; provided, however, that the acts of barking, growling, or showing of teeth by an animal shall not be sufficient to classify an animal as dangerous under this subparagraph;
(3) Killed or severely injured a domestic animal outside the attacking animal owner's property;
(4) Caused serious injury to a person resulting from reasonable attempts to escape from the animal's attack; or
(5) Has been classified as potentially dangerous or dangerous by another jurisdiction (even if that other jurisdiction uses a different term).
(b) "Vicious animal" is an animal that:
(1) Has killed a person without provocation on public or private property at any time;
(2) Has inflicted serious injury on a person being without provocation on public or private property at any time;
(3) Has caused serious injury to a person resulting from reasonable attempts to escape from the animal's attack;
(4) Has been classified as vicious by another jurisdiction (even if that other jurisdiction uses a different term); or
(5) Has been previously classified as a dangerous animal and then has:
a. Caused a substantial puncture of a person's skin by teeth without causing serious injury; provided, however, that a nip, scratch, or abrasion shall not be sufficient to classify an animal as dangerous under this section;
b. Aggressively attacked in a manner that causes a person to reasonably believe that the animal posed an imminent threat of serious injury to such person or another person although no such injury occurs; provided, however, that the acts of barking, growling, or showing of teeth by an animal shall not be sufficient to classify an animal as dangerous or vicious under this section;
c. Killed or severely injured a domestic animal outside the attacking animal owner's property; or
d. Caused serious injury to a person resulting from reasonable attempts to escape from the animal's attack.
(Ord. No. 26-002, § 1, 6-16-26)
